Test Case: network_multiple
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Missing required argument - The argument "resource_group_name" is required, but no definition was found.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The azapi.tf module call is missing the required resource_group_name parameter
- Fix Method: Add resource_group_name parameter to module call
- Changes Made: Added line 'resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.test.name' to the replicator module call in azapi.tf
- Result: Partially successful - module validation passed, but new error appeared

Attempt 2:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block is trying to access attributes on a null value. The can() function returns true even when the value is null, so the for_each creates an iteration with a null value.
- Fix Method: Add null check in the for_each condition to ensure identity is not null before iterating
- Changes Made: Changed for_each condition from 'can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [...] : []' to 'can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) && module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null ? [...] : []'
- Result: Success - Plan runs without errors, detected drifts are acceptable according to acceptable_drift_patterns.md

Final Result: Fix successful
